      "abstract": "\nIn his work The Shadow of God, Michael Rosen shows how much the authors of classical German philosophy were driven by existential questions about how to deal with suffering and evil; in particular, Hegel\u2019s philosophy of history is read as an attempt to develop a means of consolation through the concept of historical immortality. This contribution argues that Fichte, Schleiermacher, and Hegel also experiment with another attempt to offer consolation: the idea of instantaneous eternity.",
