      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "The article delivers an analysis of the image of classical German philosophy in Nelly Motroshilova\u2019s works on the history of philosophy. It is shown that Motroshilov\u2019s interpretation of German idealism is polemically directed against the stereotypical notion of its compensatory nature. According to Motroshilova, the doctrine of pure reason, which acts as the \u201ctheoretical outline\u201d of German classical philosophy, acts both as a means of realizing its own historicity and as an instrument of influencing social reality. Motroshilova\u2019s methodological approaches are close to some ideas of J\u00fcrgen Habermas, Reinhart Koselleck and Dieter Henrich. At the same time, in the image of German classical philosophy created by Motroshilova, parallels and analogies are revealed with the image of the generation of Soviet/Russian philosophers of the sixties.",
